  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Gorodetskiy is a university student. He is really good at math and really likes solving engaging math problems. In the last exam, his professor gave him really hard math problems to solve, but Gorodetskiy could not solve them and failed the exam, so the professor told him: \"These problems are a piece of cake, you should know them from school!\" Here is one of the problems from the exam - you can decide if it really was an easy problem or not.\n\nYou are given a positive integer MMM. Let's call a positive integer AAA an interesting number if there is at least one integer BBB (A≤BA \\le BA≤B) such that A⋅BA \\cdot BA⋅B is divisible by MMM and A⋅BM=A+B\\frac{A \\cdot B}{M} = A+BMA⋅B​=A+B.\n\nFind all interesting numbers. Let's denote the number of such integers by KKK; it is guaranteed that K≤3∗105K \\le 3*10^5K≤3∗105.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤M≤10141 \\le M \\le 10^{14}1≤M≤1014",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (20 points):** 1≤M≤1001 \\le M \\le 1001≤M≤100",
      "**Subtask #2 (20 points):** 1≤M≤1071 \\le M \\le 10^71≤M≤107"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer MMM.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case:\n\n\nFirst, print a line containing a single integer KKK.\nThen, print KKK lines. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines should contain a single integer ― the iii-th interesting number in increasing order.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n6",
        "output": "2\n4\n6\n5\n7\n8\n9\n10\n12",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: There are two interesting numbers, 444 and 666. For A=4A = 4A=4, we can choose B=12B = 12B=12 and for A=6A = 6A=6, we can choose B=6B = 6B=6."
      }
    ]
